# Into the Mists: the arrival on the Old Svalich Road (docs/regions/into_the_mists.md).
# Started by props on into_the_mists_road: mists_wall (the fog at the east edge) and mists_deer_carcass.

~ mist_wall
narrate examine:mists_wall
if not flag.mists_arrived
  set mists_arrived
  quest into_the_mists lost_in_mist
  -> hooks
endif
Narrator: You walk into the white, and a dozen steps later you walk out of it facing the same road in the same direction. The mist is not a wall; it is a hand, turning you around.
-> END

~ hooks
Narrator: Each of you came looking for something. None of you came looking for this.
interject name:ilse_varga: My company went into a fog like this a year ago. If this is where it took them, I'm in the right place.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: The lady in my locket called my name the whole way here. I'd like a word with her about directions.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: I dreamed of a dying sun and a silver raven. Mm. This sky looks like the first half of that dream.
interject name:silvain_aster: Aurel's last letter came out of a land of mists. Wherever this is, I'll want notes.
# Each pregen's personal quest starts here (docs/story/personal_quests.md); a custom hero in their place starts none.
if name:ilse_varga
quest kestrel_company the_letter
endif
if name:tamsin_tealeaf
quest the_locket the_dreams
endif
if name:hedda_ironvow
quest cold_prayers the_dream
endif
if name:silvain_aster
quest aurels_last_chapter the_letter
endif
if not name:ilse_varga
  interject class:fighter: Road goes one way. So do we.
endif
if not name:hedda_ironvow
  interject class:cleric: Whatever brought us here went to some trouble. That's worth remembering.
endif
* Try walking back into the mist. -> again
* Follow the road. -> END

~ again
Narrator: The mist lets you in, holds you a moment like a host taking your coat, and hands you back to the road, facing west.
interject name:silvain_aster: Not an illusion. Illusions are rude. This is courteous. I like that a great deal less.
if not name:silvain_aster
  interject class:wizard: That isn't fog. That's a border, and it has opinions.
endif
-> END

~ carcass
narrate examine:mists_deer_carcass
if flag.mists_read_the_pack
  Narrator: The kill is still here, still uneaten. The wolves that left it are still somewhere ahead.
  -> END
endif
if flag.mists_carcass_studied
  Narrator: The ground has told you all it's going to.
  -> END
endif
* [Survival DC 12] Read the tracks around it. -> carcass_tracks | carcass_no_tracks
* Leave it. -> END

~ carcass_tracks
set mists_carcass_studied
set mists_read_the_pack
Narrator: {name} reads the churned earth: a dozen wolves moving in a line, not a scatter, and a kill they never touched. They were not hungry; they were busy.
interject name:ilse_varga: That's a patrol, not a hunt. Someone's posted pickets on this road.
if not name:ilse_varga
  interject background:soldier: Wolves in a line. That's a picket. Somebody gives them orders.
endif
-> END

~ carcass_no_tracks
set mists_carcass_studied
Narrator: Prints, fog and old leaves, churned into one dark mess by something large, numerous and gone. Probably gone.
-> END
